[SIZE=5][B]0.6.0 reconstruction[/B][/SIZE]
All 51 movement paths have explicit domain owners, including recovered horizontal phase budgets, liquids, climbing, elytra and mounted packet/event evaluation. Placement variants use independent timing windows. Hitbox B consumes actual attack targets. NoSlow B and Jesus D restore detection that contradictory reference conditions prevented. Modern sulfur contact follows actual client acknowledgements.

Optional [B]checks.boatfly-a.dismount[/B], [B]checks.boatfly-b.dismount[/B], [B]checks.entityflight-a.dismount[/B], [B]checks.entityspeed-a.dismount[/B] and [B]checks.nosaddle-a.dismount[/B] are independent options under checks and default off. A cancelled violation cannot trigger dismount. Reset, logout and accepted reload cancel delayed actions. [B]checks.airplace-a.cancel[/B] controls placement interception; [B]checks.hitbox-b.maximum-angle[/B] defaults to 45 degrees.

The [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/LinoAC/blob/main/docs/FIDELITY.md]fidelity ledger[/URL] explains repairs and applicability. The [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/LinoAC/blob/main/docs/VALIDATION.md]validation report[/URL] identifies the exact JAR, finite model tests and actual Spigot/Paper runs. No comparative performance or zero-false-positive guarantee is claimed.
